Z||000010||theogre||04-01-2001||01:30 PM||||grand am brakes.... Do I realy need to say it again? Multiple Forum members have put them on the rear. Many hate them and several are planning to undo the "upgrade".<P>Autozone.com listed the rears for $30-50<P>The correct procedure for compressing the Fiero rear piston is in all the books and my cave and a bunch of threads and a dozen other places. GM does not recomend piston rotation on this caliper. It can be damaged doing so. The damage may not show up right away either. Only 88 should be rotated in.<P>Don't try to retract them by turning the screw. They may come back but you may also pop the screw out of it's seal. there is nothing holding the screw from dropping into tha caliper once the arm is off.<P>You need to reassemble the caliper before you take it in for core or they may not accept it. Depends on the store/clerk involved.<P>To do that you need help or preferably a vise. You need to push in on the piston and carefully rotate the screw slowly untill the threads grab. The help/vise is to keep the shell still while you do this.<P>once the threads grab a turn or 2 then press the piston in according to the published instructions.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-01-2001).]||||reg||1
